Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 16:22:38 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] Open the system options panel from a remote or keyboard
 button

The panel is currently reachable only by moving focus to the notification
indicator and selecting it. On a TV that is several d-pad presses from
wherever the user happens to be, and it is undiscoverable: nothing suggests
the indicator is a button.

Handle KEYCODE_SETTINGS and KEYCODE_MENU in the launcher and open the panel.
KEYCODE_SETTINGS covers remotes with a dedicated settings button;
KEYCODE_MENU covers the application key on a USB or Bluetooth keyboard, which
is what a keyboard-driven setup has available.

Add a shortcut row to the panel itself so the behaviour can be turned off,
stored in the launcher's existing default SharedPreferences alongside the
other launcher state. Turning it off removes the shortcut, not the panel: the
notification indicator still opens it, so the toggle cannot strand a user who
has just disabled the only way back in.

Defaults to on.

Change-Id: I4e05ae133b04f22f995c5aef6ea5000921b77561
